WEBVTT

1
00:00:11,813 --> 00:00:17,150
[birds chirping]

2
00:00:27,394 --> 00:00:29,564
[man]
Hey, I wanna ask you something.

3
00:00:29,998 --> 00:00:32,299
I want you to be honest,
all right?

4
00:00:33,433 --> 00:00:34,569
Okay.

5
00:00:36,336 --> 00:00:38,372
You got any regrets?

6
00:00:42,476 --> 00:00:48,683
[acoustic guitar music]

7
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:55,790
<i>♪ Oh, coal river ♪</i>

8
00:00:55,857 --> 00:01:00,127
<i>♪ Won't you wash</i>
<i>my bones away ♪</i>

9
00:01:02,462 --> 00:01:05,533
<i>♪ I'm slaving for the company ♪</i>

10
00:01:06,233 --> 00:01:09,804
<i>♪ And I can't get any pay ♪</i>

11
00:01:12,239 --> 00:01:16,010
<i>♪ Well, mining coal ♪</i>

12
00:01:16,143 --> 00:01:20,247
<i>♪ Ain't a way to make a life ♪</i>

13
00:01:21,950 --> 00:01:26,219
<i>♪ And I can't feed the hunger ♪</i>

14
00:01:26,286 --> 00:01:29,456
<i>♪ Of three kids and a wife ♪</i>

15
00:01:32,159 --> 00:01:35,495
<i>♪ Now the hollers are empty ♪</i>

16
00:01:35,563 --> 00:01:39,634
<i>♪ And the company left town ♪</i>

17
00:01:41,168 --> 00:01:45,405
<i>♪ And there ain't</i>
<i>no more mountain ♪</i>

18
00:01:47,174 --> 00:01:48,710
10-1, 10-1.

19
00:01:48,776 --> 00:01:51,445
You dead or alive down there,
buddy?

20
00:01:57,852 --> 00:02:02,289
<i>If you are dead,</i>
<i>can I keep the truck? Over.</i>

21
00:02:03,190 --> 00:02:04,358
[walkie-talkie crackles]

22
00:02:04,424 --> 00:02:06,259
I'm in the main tunnel.

23
00:02:06,326 --> 00:02:08,630
Ain't no one been in here
in a hundred years

24
00:02:09,329 --> 00:02:11,532
And no you don't get
to keep no damn truck.

25
00:02:12,199 --> 00:02:13,601
Over.

26
00:02:14,769 --> 00:02:17,538
<i>-What's it like down there?</i>
-[debris falling]

27
00:02:18,338 --> 00:02:21,676
-It's spooky. Over.
-[walkie-talkie crackles]

28
00:02:21,743 --> 00:02:25,580
<i>Keep your eyes on the prize,</i>
<i>brother. Nut up and shut up!</i>

29
00:02:25,647 --> 00:02:27,381
- <i>Over.</i>
-[walkie-talkie crackles]

30
00:02:32,987 --> 00:02:34,756
Easy for you to say.

31
00:02:50,872 --> 00:02:56,878
[ominous music]

32
00:03:14,327 --> 00:03:17,899
[chain rattles]

33
00:03:17,965 --> 00:03:23,705
[ominous music]

34
00:03:26,974 --> 00:03:29,610
[faint rustling]

35
00:03:30,712 --> 00:03:32,279
[water dripping]

36
00:03:50,665 --> 00:03:54,468
-[walkie-talkie crackles]
-Some strange shit down here.

37
00:03:55,670 --> 00:03:59,306
But there's coal, alright.
Over.

38
00:03:59,306 --> 00:04:03,845
<i>Hallelujah,</i>
<i>how much we talking?</i>
<i>Over.</i>

39
00:04:03,911 --> 00:04:07,414
Sealed shut.
Old gas seal, maybe.

40
00:04:09,851 --> 00:04:14,454
[ominous music]

41
00:04:14,522 --> 00:04:16,389
<i>Jesse, you copy?</i>

42
00:04:16,456 --> 00:04:17,759
There's something...

43
00:04:19,127 --> 00:04:21,028
Something is inside there.

44
00:04:21,095 --> 00:04:25,633
[ominous music builds]

45
00:04:28,368 --> 00:04:29,570
[door creaks]

46
00:04:29,637 --> 00:04:31,606
[boom and rumbling]

47
00:04:31,672 --> 00:04:35,475
[over walkie-talkie] <i>Jesse,</i>
<i>get the hell out of there,</i>
<i>Jesse!</i>

48
00:04:36,177 --> 00:04:42,016
[ominous music builds]

49
00:04:53,261 --> 00:04:56,731
[explosion]

50
00:05:38,506 --> 00:05:41,142
[child imitates engine revving]

51
00:05:41,909 --> 00:05:45,079
[woman] <i>You've seen with your</i>
<i>own eyes what they're doing</i>
<i>next door at Rock Creek.</i>

52
00:05:46,514 --> 00:05:48,481
<i>Dynamiting the mountain.</i>

53
00:05:48,549 --> 00:05:51,619
<i>-Spitting lead into the air.</i>
-[rumbling]

54
00:05:51,686 --> 00:05:53,621
Arsenic into the river.

55
00:05:53,688 --> 00:05:55,623
They ain't here to hire us.

56
00:05:55,690 --> 00:05:57,225
They're here for the land.

57
00:05:57,291 --> 00:05:58,626
So we get new homes.

58
00:05:59,227 --> 00:06:01,529
Ain't nothing special about
this holler over any other.

59
00:06:01,596 --> 00:06:03,698
We got elderly.
We got young.

60
00:06:03,764 --> 00:06:05,566
Not everybody can up
and move on.

61
00:06:05,633 --> 00:06:07,467
[Bo] When we got money.
We'll figure it out.

62
00:06:07,535 --> 00:06:08,936
[distant explosion]

63
00:06:17,044 --> 00:06:19,113
I got offered 50 large.

64
00:06:20,248 --> 00:06:24,285
Now when am I gonna see
another $50,000
in this lifetime?

65
00:06:24,352 --> 00:06:26,354
If you sell,

66
00:06:26,453 --> 00:06:28,356
if any of us sells,

67
00:06:28,455 --> 00:06:31,692
they'll use court precedent
to sue to get the rest
of the plots,

68
00:06:31,759 --> 00:06:33,761
just like they done at Hobet.

69
00:06:33,828 --> 00:06:35,830
Now maybe you get 50 grand
in your pocket,

70
00:06:35,897 --> 00:06:40,467
but the rest of us,
we'll be lucky if we get five.

71
00:06:40,467 --> 00:06:42,003
You gonna sell out your Ma?

72
00:06:42,970 --> 00:06:44,205
Your cousin?

73
00:06:44,839 --> 00:06:47,675
-Your uncle on the plot over?
-KC.

74
00:06:48,576 --> 00:06:51,112
Your folks've been here
longer than any of us.

75
00:06:52,146 --> 00:06:53,681
What do you say?

76
00:06:59,754 --> 00:07:02,523
I saw coal dust
on the patio today.

77
00:07:03,824 --> 00:07:07,094
Coming down out of the sky
like it was snow.

78
00:07:08,629 --> 00:07:11,732
The same black dust that
got into my daddy's lungs.

79
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:15,870
Chase, he turns ten tomorrow.

80
00:07:17,271 --> 00:07:19,540
He was out there playing in it.

81
00:07:20,341 --> 00:07:21,842
It ain't right.

82
00:07:23,244 --> 00:07:26,614
[somber music]

83
00:07:28,883 --> 00:07:30,885
We'll put it to a vote.

84
00:07:34,288 --> 00:07:40,528
[ominous music]

85
00:08:00,047 --> 00:08:02,216
[on TV] <i>Just two hours ago,</i>
<i>Allied Air Forces</i>

86
00:08:02,283 --> 00:08:06,620
<i>began its attack on military</i>
<i>targets in Iraq and Kuwait.</i>

87
00:08:06,687 --> 00:08:09,023
<i>These attacks continue</i>
<i>as I speak.</i>

88
00:08:09,090 --> 00:08:10,257
Hey, Meemaw.

89
00:08:10,324 --> 00:08:12,560
[on TV] <i>Ground forces</i>
<i>are not engaged.</i>

90
00:08:13,194 --> 00:08:15,096
<i>This conflict started</i>
<i>August 7th.</i>

91
00:08:15,162 --> 00:08:16,263
[mailbox opens]

92
00:08:18,199 --> 00:08:20,901
[on TV] <i>...a small and helpless</i>
<i>neighbor.</i>

93
00:08:20,968 --> 00:08:23,971
<i>Kuwait, a member</i>
<i>of the Arab League...</i>

94
00:08:24,038 --> 00:08:27,141
-[KC] Any good news?
-[on TV] <i>...was crushed.</i>

95
00:08:31,846 --> 00:08:34,081
[explosion, ground shaking]

96
00:08:34,148 --> 00:08:36,117
[utensils clatter]

97
00:08:38,919 --> 00:08:43,324
[on TV] <i>We will also destroy</i>
<i>his chemical weapons</i>
<i>facilities.</i>

98
00:08:43,391 --> 00:08:47,862
[wind howls]

99
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:56,604
[distant explosion]

100
00:09:08,182 --> 00:09:09,717
[distant explosion]

101
00:09:09,784 --> 00:09:12,653
[birds chirping]

102
00:09:23,764 --> 00:09:25,733
[lighter ignites]

103
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:27,101
[lighter snaps shut]

104
00:09:28,402 --> 00:09:29,837
Thanks.

105
00:09:34,708 --> 00:09:36,310
What if we did get out?

106
00:09:39,647 --> 00:09:41,148
You heard Doc.

107
00:09:42,517 --> 00:09:44,852
We'd be selling out everyone
we know.

108
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:49,056
Josie can't travel,
not with her lungs.

109
00:09:55,496 --> 00:09:59,233
But this here land might
be worth a lot more than
they're letting on.

110
00:10:03,003 --> 00:10:06,340
[Jesse] I went down that old
wildcat mine down the holler.

111
00:10:08,676 --> 00:10:11,212
There's coal down there, KC,
maybe a lot.

112
00:10:14,782 --> 00:10:17,118
You went down there
and you didn't tell me?

113
00:10:17,184 --> 00:10:20,855
Look, you said you're worried
about Chase.
I am too. I just...

114
00:10:21,822 --> 00:10:23,724
I want to know our options.

115
00:10:34,335 --> 00:10:35,769
I'm sorry, alright?

116
00:10:38,839 --> 00:10:40,307
I should have told you.

117
00:10:42,176 --> 00:10:46,147
This here's your family land.
You gotta be the one to decide.

118
00:10:49,016 --> 00:10:51,185
This is the only home
I've ever known.

119
00:10:54,655 --> 00:10:57,658
To let them win after
all they've done?

120
00:11:02,229 --> 00:11:03,464
[insect buzzing]

121
00:11:03,532 --> 00:11:05,299
We gonna figure it out.

122
00:11:20,981 --> 00:11:23,817
Don't you go down
that mine again.

123
00:11:26,787 --> 00:11:28,255
I won't.

124
00:11:32,561 --> 00:11:34,094
Promise me.

125
00:11:36,330 --> 00:11:39,133
Yeah, I do.

126
00:11:43,538 --> 00:11:44,838
Okay.

127
00:11:53,380 --> 00:11:55,883
[uplifting music]

128
00:11:57,785 --> 00:11:59,386
You're annoying.

129
00:12:00,421 --> 00:12:01,789
[laughs]

130
00:12:03,490 --> 00:12:09,496
[uplifting music continues]

131
00:12:20,542 --> 00:12:22,910
[coughing]

132
00:12:30,685 --> 00:12:32,453
You all right, bud?

133
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:34,355
[coughs]

134
00:12:35,089 --> 00:12:38,225
Alright.
It's your birthday tomorrow

135
00:12:38,292 --> 00:12:40,562
You're gonna be ten years old.

136
00:12:40,629 --> 00:12:42,564
Imagine that.

137
00:12:42,631 --> 00:12:46,000
How about you and me,
we go down the New River gorge

138
00:12:46,066 --> 00:12:48,235
tomorrow and catch some trout?

139
00:12:48,302 --> 00:12:49,638
Okay.

140
00:12:49,704 --> 00:12:51,005
[coughs]

141
00:12:52,439 --> 00:12:57,211
[music intensifies]

142
00:12:57,278 --> 00:13:00,047
[coughs heavily]

143
00:13:02,517 --> 00:13:05,419
[coughing continues]

144
00:13:12,459 --> 00:13:15,362
[explosion]

145
00:13:20,067 --> 00:13:21,636
[machines clatter]

146
00:13:21,703 --> 00:13:24,905
[Jesse] <i>We got some back taxes</i>
<i>we can't can't pay.</i>

147
00:13:27,474 --> 00:13:30,044
<i>Bank is threatening</i>
<i>foreclosure.</i>

148
00:13:32,479 --> 00:13:34,181
[rattling]

149
00:13:37,184 --> 00:13:39,253
Look, son, I'mma level with you.

150
00:13:40,287 --> 00:13:42,890
The price on condemned land,

151
00:13:42,890 --> 00:13:44,892
if we take it through
eminent domain,

152
00:13:44,892 --> 00:13:46,460
it ain't much.

153
00:13:47,127 --> 00:13:50,030
But if there is coal
underneath there,

154
00:13:50,097 --> 00:13:52,600
and we can do a direct sale,

155
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:56,504
well then we can talk turkey!
[laughs]

156
00:13:58,339 --> 00:14:00,007
KC would never agree to that.

157
00:14:00,074 --> 00:14:01,576
[Lawson] That's a damn shame.

158
00:14:03,010 --> 00:14:04,311
[clears throat]

159
00:14:06,046 --> 00:14:07,816
Hey, do you hunt?

160
00:14:07,915 --> 00:14:10,250
-Buck season's coming up.
-Yeah.

161
00:14:10,317 --> 00:14:12,486
[Lawson]
Well, let me show you something.

162
00:14:12,554 --> 00:14:13,655
[clears throat]

163
00:14:14,221 --> 00:14:17,559
6.3 tons on that big boy!

164
00:14:17,625 --> 00:14:19,226
Can you believe that?

165
00:14:19,993 --> 00:14:21,395
[Lawson]
See, that right there is me,

166
00:14:21,462 --> 00:14:23,330
and that man next to me,
you might recognize

167
00:14:23,397 --> 00:14:27,602
from being on TV on account
that he sits on the US Senate.

168
00:14:27,669 --> 00:14:30,572
Have you ever been on a safari,
Jesse?

169
00:14:31,673 --> 00:14:32,940
[scoffs]

170
00:14:33,006 --> 00:14:34,776
-No.
-No.

171
00:14:34,843 --> 00:14:38,713
No, I figure you ain't never
even left the county. Have you?

172
00:14:38,780 --> 00:14:40,280
That right?

173
00:14:40,347 --> 00:14:42,950
Hell, you can't even pay
your mortgage.

174
00:14:50,090 --> 00:14:51,458
Fuck this.

175
00:14:53,127 --> 00:14:54,361
[camera thuds]

176
00:14:54,428 --> 00:14:57,197
-What's that?
-That is an offer.

177
00:14:59,701 --> 00:15:02,069
[Lawson]
Look, son, we're gonna
take the land either way.

178
00:15:03,738 --> 00:15:05,372
Just a matter of when.

179
00:15:06,541 --> 00:15:08,743
And how long before
that bank moves in?

180
00:15:08,810 --> 00:15:10,612
What? A few weeks?

181
00:15:10,678 --> 00:15:13,748
And they gonna take it anyway.

182
00:15:14,281 --> 00:15:16,984
And leave you with nothing?

183
00:15:18,185 --> 00:15:21,155
Just help us get what we need,
Jesse.

184
00:15:21,221 --> 00:15:23,558
And you'll be compensated.

185
00:15:24,124 --> 00:15:26,126
And the real question is,

186
00:15:26,193 --> 00:15:29,898
how can you go home
and look that pretty little wife

187
00:15:29,997 --> 00:15:32,099
of yours in the eye
if you don't?

188
00:15:34,903 --> 00:15:36,571
[ground shakes]

189
00:15:36,638 --> 00:15:42,644
<i>♪ Dark is the coal dust</i>
<i>and deepest of night ♪</i>

190
00:15:42,710 --> 00:15:47,549
<i>♪ The only grave</i>
<i>you will know ♪</i>

191
00:15:48,516 --> 00:15:52,019
<i>♪ For the cold night</i>
<i>is coming ♪</i>

192
00:15:52,085 --> 00:15:54,756
<i>♪ It'll call you inside ♪</i>

193
00:15:55,422 --> 00:16:00,360
<i>♪ And fill you with trouble ♪</i>

194
00:16:06,568 --> 00:16:08,135
What are you doing?

195
00:16:11,038 --> 00:16:13,340
<i>♪ Dark is the coal dust ♪</i>

196
00:16:13,407 --> 00:16:16,511
<i>♪ That burns in your lungs ♪</i>

197
00:16:16,578 --> 00:16:21,081
<i>♪ The only breath</i>
<i>you will know ♪</i>

198
00:16:22,382 --> 00:16:24,786
<i>♪ For the old dark is coming ♪</i>

199
00:16:25,352 --> 00:16:28,890
<i>♪ It'll turn you to stone ♪</i>

200
00:16:28,957 --> 00:16:32,493
<i>♪ And fill you with trouble ♪</i>

201
00:16:32,560 --> 00:16:34,629
[explosion]

202
00:16:36,096 --> 00:16:39,366
[debris falling]

203
00:17:01,188 --> 00:17:02,857
<i>♪ Come home ♪</i>

204
00:17:03,457 --> 00:17:06,493
<i>♪ Come home ♪</i>

205
00:17:06,561 --> 00:17:12,165
<i>♪ Come home to your love ♪</i>

206
00:17:12,232 --> 00:17:13,868
[paper burns]

207
00:17:13,935 --> 00:17:19,106
<i>♪ I'll feel the fire that burns</i>
<i>in your eyes ♪</i>

208
00:17:19,172 --> 00:17:23,377
<i>♪ And leave all your ♪</i>

209
00:17:23,443 --> 00:17:26,113
<i>♪ Trouble ♪</i>

210
00:17:52,272 --> 00:17:53,741
Time for bed.

211
00:17:53,808 --> 00:17:55,442
But I wanna go fishing.

212
00:17:58,880 --> 00:18:00,314
What did I tell you?

213
00:18:01,315 --> 00:18:05,152
[sighs] If ifs and buts
were candy and nuts,

214
00:18:05,152 --> 00:18:07,722
every day would be Christmas.

215
00:18:07,789 --> 00:18:09,156
That's right.

216
00:18:15,162 --> 00:18:16,396
Go.

217
00:18:31,813 --> 00:18:35,583
[TV playing]

218
00:18:38,920 --> 00:18:41,488
-[object rattles]
-I don't wanna hear it.

219
00:18:41,556 --> 00:18:44,358
You've been waiting to say
"I told you so" since the day
we were married.

220
00:18:44,424 --> 00:18:46,393
So what? He dealt a little dope
when he was a kid.

221
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:48,630
Did a little time.
Who didn't around here?

222
00:18:48,696 --> 00:18:49,831
[dishes rattle]

223
00:18:51,365 --> 00:18:53,433
-I'm gonna go look for him.
-[object rattles]

224
00:18:53,500 --> 00:18:54,936
That ain't kind
and that ain't true.

225
00:18:55,670 --> 00:18:58,072
-[bell jingles]
-We'll talk when you can
be nice.

226
00:18:58,205 --> 00:19:00,240
[object rattles heavily]

227
00:19:00,307 --> 00:19:06,514
[ominous music]

228
00:19:16,024 --> 00:19:18,225
[engine shuts off]

229
00:19:20,460 --> 00:19:23,230
[loud music playing]

230
00:19:26,034 --> 00:19:27,334
[knock on door]

231
00:19:30,270 --> 00:19:31,973
[knocks heavily]

232
00:19:32,040 --> 00:19:34,341
[loud music continues]

233
00:19:35,076 --> 00:19:37,111
Is Jesse in there?

234
00:19:37,244 --> 00:19:39,514
-Why don't you fuck off?
-[door slams]

235
00:19:42,850 --> 00:19:44,819
Jesus, KC!

236
00:19:44,886 --> 00:19:46,286
I told you, he ain't here.

237
00:19:46,988 --> 00:19:48,255
How old is she?

238
00:19:48,255 --> 00:19:49,924
How am I supposed to know?

239
00:19:49,991 --> 00:19:51,959
Maybe when we go ask
Sheriff Henley, then?

240
00:19:52,026 --> 00:19:53,260
Hey, that ain't funny.

241
00:19:53,326 --> 00:19:55,563
Do I look like a fucking clown?

242
00:19:59,266 --> 00:20:02,070
-He's with Bo Brown. Okay?
-Where?

243
00:20:02,136 --> 00:20:04,739
Jesus, KC. I don't know.

244
00:20:04,806 --> 00:20:05,973
Probably drunk.

245
00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:08,710
He'd be home sooner if
you quit hounding him.

246
00:20:08,776 --> 00:20:12,847
Hey, look, I didn't sell
nothing, okay? I swear.

247
00:20:13,881 --> 00:20:15,348
Don't you start.

248
00:20:34,535 --> 00:20:36,303
Shit, Jesse. What did you do?

249
00:20:36,369 --> 00:20:38,371
[car engine turns on]

250
00:20:41,109 --> 00:20:43,310
[heavy object thuds]

251
00:20:43,376 --> 00:20:45,913
[water drips]

252
00:20:45,980 --> 00:20:47,782
[heavy object thuds]

253
00:20:55,189 --> 00:20:58,458
[door creaks]

254
00:21:12,472 --> 00:21:15,009
[Jesse] You got the carbon
monoxide detector?

255
00:21:15,076 --> 00:21:16,376
About that...

256
00:21:17,377 --> 00:21:19,080
[Bo] Woah now, settle down.

257
00:21:19,147 --> 00:21:20,848
What the hell you got in there?

258
00:21:20,915 --> 00:21:23,518
I couldn't get my hands
on a CMD.

259
00:21:23,584 --> 00:21:26,788
So I brung old Dusky here.

260
00:21:26,854 --> 00:21:27,955
[cat meows]

261
00:21:29,257 --> 00:21:31,592
That's a cat, Bo.

262
00:21:31,659 --> 00:21:34,829
Yeah. Ain't you never heard
of a cat in a coal mine?

263
00:21:34,896 --> 00:21:38,199
It's a canary, dumbass.
It's a bird.

264
00:21:38,266 --> 00:21:40,902
Yeah, I caught me a bird too.

265
00:21:40,968 --> 00:21:42,670
But Dusky ate it.

266
00:21:42,737 --> 00:21:46,541
Anyway, I figure it's
the same in principle.

267
00:21:46,607 --> 00:21:48,976
-[cat growls]
-Out your damn gourd.

268
00:21:56,416 --> 00:21:58,219
Well come on.

269
00:21:58,286 --> 00:21:59,987
Well, maybe I should stay here.

270
00:22:02,824 --> 00:22:04,391
[cat meows]

271
00:22:07,494 --> 00:22:08,796
Give me the cat then.

272
00:22:09,396 --> 00:22:10,698
Why?

273
00:22:12,133 --> 00:22:14,035
Because what if there's gas?

274
00:22:15,402 --> 00:22:17,905
I don't want no harm
to come to her.

275
00:22:17,972 --> 00:22:19,140
It's Dusky.

276
00:22:19,207 --> 00:22:21,509
-Bo, give me the cat.
-No.

277
00:22:21,576 --> 00:22:23,410
Give me the cat, Bo.
Give me the cat.

278
00:22:23,476 --> 00:22:25,079
You're scaring her.

279
00:22:25,146 --> 00:22:26,647
[cat meows]

280
00:22:26,714 --> 00:22:29,016
-[water drips]
-[cat meows]

281
00:22:31,451 --> 00:22:34,188
-[cat meows]
-It's okay, Dusky.

282
00:22:34,255 --> 00:22:35,422
It's all right.

283
00:22:35,455 --> 00:22:37,091
[rope tightens]

284
00:22:40,261 --> 00:22:44,431
[ominous music]

285
00:22:44,431 --> 00:22:46,667
Tug twice if you get in trouble.

286
00:22:55,743 --> 00:22:57,477
This place is huge.

287
00:23:00,447 --> 00:23:02,116
[Bo] You see any coal?

288
00:23:10,291 --> 00:23:14,929
[ominous music continues]

289
00:23:16,463 --> 00:23:18,498
It's all coal.

290
00:23:28,676 --> 00:23:30,011
[camera shutter clicks]

291
00:24:09,517 --> 00:24:10,851
[camera shutter clicks]

292
00:24:12,520 --> 00:24:18,726
[ominous music continues]

293
00:24:24,098 --> 00:24:29,103
[music intensifies]

294
00:24:29,170 --> 00:24:30,538
[debris clatters]

295
00:24:34,542 --> 00:24:36,077
Bo?

296
00:24:36,143 --> 00:24:39,313
[ominous music]

297
00:24:39,380 --> 00:24:40,681
Is that you?

298
00:24:56,263 --> 00:24:58,933
Well lookie here.

299
00:25:05,072 --> 00:25:07,208
-Finders keepers.
-[cat meows]

300
00:25:07,274 --> 00:25:08,843
Oh!

301
00:25:08,909 --> 00:25:10,444
Dusky.

302
00:25:10,578 --> 00:25:11,645
[ground rumbles]

303
00:25:11,712 --> 00:25:14,749
[rope tightens]

304
00:25:19,153 --> 00:25:20,454
Oh, shit.

305
00:25:20,588 --> 00:25:21,822
[rope snaps]

306
00:25:21,889 --> 00:25:28,095
[music intensifies]

307
00:25:29,830 --> 00:25:36,037
[ominous music]

308
00:25:41,609 --> 00:25:45,746
[footsteps approaching]

309
00:25:47,448 --> 00:25:48,749
[Bo] Oh, shit!

310
00:25:53,054 --> 00:25:56,991
[screaming]

311
00:26:13,941 --> 00:26:15,910
[KC] <i>He's been missing</i>
<i>since yesterday.</i>

312
00:26:18,012 --> 00:26:20,147
Well, how long do I
gotta wait to report it?

313
00:26:22,950 --> 00:26:24,718
Look, it ain't like him.

314
00:26:28,422 --> 00:26:29,790
Yeah.

315
00:26:30,658 --> 00:26:32,026
Yeah, okay.

316
00:26:33,360 --> 00:26:34,728
I understand.

317
00:26:37,698 --> 00:26:39,033
Shit.

318
00:26:40,668 --> 00:26:42,571
[vehicles approaching]

319
00:26:42,670 --> 00:26:44,672
What the hell?

320
00:26:47,208 --> 00:26:53,214
[ominous music]

321
00:26:57,852 --> 00:27:01,255
[trucks pass by]

322
00:27:18,573 --> 00:27:24,778
[ominous music]

323
00:27:38,292 --> 00:27:40,261
[miners talking]

324
00:27:40,327 --> 00:27:41,428
Hey!

325
00:27:46,500 --> 00:27:49,003
Well, howdy, ma'am.
This here's a company mine.

326
00:27:49,069 --> 00:27:52,473
For right now, I'm gonna have
to ask you to keep off
the property.

327
00:27:52,541 --> 00:27:54,808
You're Dorsey Cayton.

328
00:27:54,875 --> 00:27:57,044
You used to drive
with my daddy Jeb.

329
00:27:58,412 --> 00:28:00,281
You must be KC.

330
00:28:00,347 --> 00:28:01,916
Yeah.

331
00:28:01,982 --> 00:28:04,151
So you know for a fact that
this ain't your land,

332
00:28:04,218 --> 00:28:06,787
and you
got no right to be here.

333
00:28:08,122 --> 00:28:10,758
All I know is what's
right here in black and white.

334
00:28:10,758 --> 00:28:14,361
You can take it up with the home
office, but I can't do nothin'
for ya.

335
00:28:15,396 --> 00:28:16,897
And I can't let you pass.

336
00:28:16,964 --> 00:28:19,601
-Is Jesse in there?
-[Dorsey] Jesse?

337
00:28:19,668 --> 00:28:21,435
What you want with that junkie?

338
00:28:22,403 --> 00:28:23,804
Wait...

339
00:28:23,871 --> 00:28:25,607
Don't tell me you went
and married him.

340
00:28:25,674 --> 00:28:29,276
[laughs]

341
00:28:30,878 --> 00:28:32,279
Hey, I'm kiddin'.

342
00:28:32,346 --> 00:28:33,948
What's the matter?
You can't take a fuckin' joke?

343
00:28:34,014 --> 00:28:35,382
Get out of my way.

344
00:28:36,383 --> 00:28:37,586
[body thuds]

345
00:28:37,652 --> 00:28:41,355
[grunts in pain]

346
00:28:41,422 --> 00:28:44,458
You know, they used to
talk about you on the pit.

347
00:28:44,526 --> 00:28:47,696
Jeb's little girl had
something of a reputation.

348
00:28:47,795 --> 00:28:49,797
A real fuckin' skank!

349
00:28:49,863 --> 00:28:51,566
Fuck you.

350
00:28:51,633 --> 00:28:55,803
What I heard, you like to
squeal like a stuck fuckin' pig!

351
00:28:55,836 --> 00:28:59,940
[Dorsey imitates snorting]

352
00:29:00,808 --> 00:29:02,376
[hooting and hollering]

353
00:29:04,378 --> 00:29:05,714
[truck approaching]

354
00:29:05,813 --> 00:29:07,147
[truck engine stops]

355
00:29:08,148 --> 00:29:11,151
Oh, hi. Ma'am, can you just
have a seat in the corner?

356
00:29:11,819 --> 00:29:13,320
Ma'am, excuse me.

357
00:29:13,387 --> 00:29:14,822
Ma'am, excuse me.

358
00:29:14,855 --> 00:29:16,390
Your goddamn thugs
are on my land,

359
00:29:16,457 --> 00:29:17,992
and my goddamn husband
is missin'.

360
00:29:18,058 --> 00:29:20,094
[receptionist]
I am so sorry, sir.

361
00:29:21,730 --> 00:29:25,899
KC, we've been tryin' to
get hold of you.

362
00:29:25,966 --> 00:29:29,069
-Why don't you sit down?
-Where's Jesse?

363
00:29:29,136 --> 00:29:30,938
Sit?

364
00:29:31,005 --> 00:29:32,339
For my sake.

365
00:29:38,479 --> 00:29:41,382
Now listen, I don't know how
to tell you this,

366
00:29:41,448 --> 00:29:45,352
but it seems like you ain't
got word, so here it is.

367
00:29:46,453 --> 00:29:50,157
I got a call a few hours ago
from the boys runnin' GPR.

368
00:29:51,526 --> 00:29:55,963
Your Jesse was in that mine
during a partial collapse.

369
00:29:58,365 --> 00:30:00,234
-What?
-Now I want you to know

370
00:30:00,301 --> 00:30:04,606
I am doing
everything in my power
to try to save that boy.

371
00:30:04,673 --> 00:30:06,373
Did you send him down there?

372
00:30:06,440 --> 00:30:10,244
-Point of fact, he volunteered.
-You're lying.

373
00:30:10,311 --> 00:30:13,648
And even if you ain't,
I want you off my land.

374
00:30:13,715 --> 00:30:15,316
I'll find him myself.

375
00:30:16,250 --> 00:30:18,218
Look, let me put this
to you simple.

376
00:30:19,754 --> 00:30:20,988
[paper rustles]

377
00:30:21,055 --> 00:30:22,990
It ain't your land no more, KC.

378
00:30:23,057 --> 00:30:25,959
I made Jesse an offer,
and he took it.

379
00:30:26,026 --> 00:30:27,494
[paper rustles sharply]

380
00:30:30,699 --> 00:30:31,932
[paper crumples]

381
00:30:31,999 --> 00:30:33,500
That's all right, we got copies.

382
00:30:33,568 --> 00:30:35,336
It's a fuckin' forgery.

383
00:30:35,969 --> 00:30:38,405
-Prove it.
-I will, I'll sue you.

384
00:30:38,472 --> 00:30:42,042
Mm-hmm. Yeah, and it'll be
your word against his.

385
00:30:42,610 --> 00:30:45,714
And without him there
in court to testify,

386
00:30:45,780 --> 00:30:48,882
well, good luck.

387
00:30:48,949 --> 00:30:51,185
[distant explosion]

388
00:30:54,388 --> 00:30:55,590
[bangs table]

389
00:31:12,540 --> 00:31:13,941
[car door slams]

390
00:31:19,947 --> 00:31:21,248
Fuck.

391
00:31:23,651 --> 00:31:25,018
[grunts]

392
00:31:27,121 --> 00:31:28,523
[heavy breathing]

393
00:31:29,957 --> 00:31:31,358
[heavy breathing]

394
00:31:32,493 --> 00:31:33,961
[heavy breathing]

395
00:31:45,973 --> 00:31:52,179
[sobbing]

396
00:32:03,090 --> 00:32:06,126
[TV playing]

397
00:32:10,164 --> 00:32:12,534
[on TV]
<i>You know, it's hard to believe.</i>

398
00:32:12,600 --> 00:32:16,103
<i>It's hard to believe</i>
<i>when we haven't kept</i>

399
00:32:16,170 --> 00:32:18,506
<i>this issue from every time.</i>

400
00:32:18,573 --> 00:32:24,077
<i>When we have men</i>
<i>and women standing</i>
<i>preaching and teaching,</i>

401
00:32:24,144 --> 00:32:29,918
<i>it is hard to believe that men</i>
<i>are at low sight on heaven</i>

402
00:32:30,017 --> 00:32:32,119
<i>and that's about a good boy.</i>

403
00:32:33,555 --> 00:32:35,355
[coughing]

404
00:32:35,422 --> 00:32:36,524
[coughing]

405
00:32:39,828 --> 00:32:41,462
Told you so.

406
00:32:44,097 --> 00:32:49,236
[TV continues playing]

407
00:32:52,507 --> 00:32:54,174
[phone ringing]

408
00:32:56,778 --> 00:32:59,246
[phone ringing]

409
00:33:12,059 --> 00:33:14,261
Manhattan is expecting a report.

410
00:33:14,762 --> 00:33:17,397
You know what's at stake
for our investors.

411
00:33:17,464 --> 00:33:21,468
Now look, things work
different down here.

412
00:33:22,469 --> 00:33:25,607
You gotta work the people.

413
00:33:25,673 --> 00:33:31,679
Our bosses know this and that is
why they put me in charge of it.

414
00:33:32,981 --> 00:33:35,082
Results, Lawson.

415
00:33:43,257 --> 00:33:49,129
[crickets chirping]

416
00:34:05,178 --> 00:34:06,514
[paper rustles]

417
00:34:39,146 --> 00:34:40,548
Jesse?

418
00:34:47,755 --> 00:34:50,558
[crickets chirping]

419
00:34:50,625 --> 00:34:51,859
Hey, who's there?

420
00:34:55,830 --> 00:35:01,836
[eerie music]

421
00:35:28,630 --> 00:35:30,765
[snarling]

422
00:35:38,940 --> 00:35:40,240
[panting]

423
00:35:40,307 --> 00:35:41,475
-[Jesse] KC help me
-[KC] No!

424
00:35:41,542 --> 00:35:43,611
Help me
Help me, KC! Help me!

425
00:35:43,678 --> 00:35:46,681
-Help me KC, please!
-[screaming]

426
00:35:50,217 --> 00:35:53,788
[coughing]

427
00:35:55,056 --> 00:35:58,693
[coughing]

428
00:36:16,878 --> 00:36:21,314
[gasping]

429
00:36:21,381 --> 00:36:24,451
[rain pattering]

430
00:36:39,867 --> 00:36:42,436
[lightning crashing]

431
00:36:47,274 --> 00:36:48,776
Chase!

432
00:36:50,845 --> 00:36:52,279
Chase!

433
00:36:52,345 --> 00:36:54,381
Hey, hey, little bean.

434
00:36:54,448 --> 00:36:55,817
Little bean, come on.

435
00:36:58,619 --> 00:37:02,355
You're all right.
You're all right. Hey, Come on.

436
00:37:08,295 --> 00:37:09,864
Hold still, it's gonna sting,
okay?

437
00:37:09,931 --> 00:37:11,298
Okay.

438
00:37:25,046 --> 00:37:26,480
What's this?

439
00:37:31,219 --> 00:37:37,424
[ominous music]

440
00:37:41,328 --> 00:37:42,830
Where did you get this?

441
00:37:45,800 --> 00:37:47,001
Chase.

442
00:37:47,068 --> 00:37:48,870
The coal man gave it to me.

443
00:37:51,371 --> 00:37:53,975
-[distant thunder rumbling]
-Okay.

444
00:37:56,110 --> 00:37:57,745
Let's get you back to bed, okay?

445
00:37:57,812 --> 00:37:58,913
Okay.

446
00:38:02,917 --> 00:38:05,352
[birds chirping]

447
00:38:46,928 --> 00:38:48,663
[squelching]

448
00:38:59,073 --> 00:39:05,079
[wind blowing]

449
00:39:11,986 --> 00:39:13,554
[birds chirping]

450
00:39:17,424 --> 00:39:19,426
Hey, open up.

451
00:39:23,331 --> 00:39:24,832
[door creaks]

452
00:39:30,938 --> 00:39:32,439
[door creaks]

453
00:39:49,456 --> 00:39:50,691
Cricket?

454
00:40:20,054 --> 00:40:23,490
[shaky breathing]

455
00:40:36,469 --> 00:40:40,675
[gasping]

456
00:40:51,886 --> 00:40:53,087
[sniffs]

457
00:41:04,565 --> 00:41:06,033
Jesse's in trouble.

458
00:41:06,767 --> 00:41:08,869
We gotta warn him.

459
00:41:09,637 --> 00:41:11,072
It's too late.

460
00:41:11,572 --> 00:41:13,607
He and Bo got trapped down
a Mine Shaft.

461
00:41:13,674 --> 00:41:15,343
-It can't be.
-Well, it is.

462
00:41:15,409 --> 00:41:18,145
It ain't KC, Bo was here.

463
00:41:22,383 --> 00:41:24,652
Last night he came in,

464
00:41:24,719 --> 00:41:26,821
coughing, hacking up a lung.

465
00:41:26,887 --> 00:41:29,824
He was begging me for a hit,
scared as shit.

466
00:41:30,858 --> 00:41:32,793
I think he got me sick.

467
00:41:32,860 --> 00:41:34,662
Where the hell is he now?

468
00:41:34,729 --> 00:41:38,599
I called the Black Lung
Clinic and they,
they came and took him.

469
00:41:38,666 --> 00:41:40,201
The one up in Kingwood?

470
00:41:41,869 --> 00:41:45,239
-I gotta go.
-KC, you been dreaming?

471
00:41:46,173 --> 00:41:48,242
I've been having this one
over and over.

472
00:41:48,309 --> 00:41:49,610
It's, it's dark.

473
00:41:49,677 --> 00:41:51,912
It's-- it's like my feet
sliding into the ground.

474
00:41:51,979 --> 00:41:54,115
Like, like,
like it's pulling me in.

475
00:41:54,181 --> 00:41:56,484
In this dream,
something's hunting me.

476
00:41:56,584 --> 00:41:59,120
Something from down in the
mountain hollers or some--

477
00:42:01,055 --> 00:42:02,223
It ain't human.

478
00:42:08,763 --> 00:42:10,164
Get some rest.

479
00:42:22,777 --> 00:42:28,983
[ominous music]

480
00:42:37,691 --> 00:42:39,226
[coughing]

481
00:42:40,027 --> 00:42:41,162
[breathing]

482
00:42:51,072 --> 00:42:52,740
[receptionist]
Breathing center.

483
00:42:55,643 --> 00:43:01,849
[distant coughs]

484
00:43:05,486 --> 00:43:09,890
[distant coughs]

485
00:43:13,562 --> 00:43:17,331
[machine beeping]

486
00:43:31,145 --> 00:43:32,947
Oh, shit, Bo.

487
00:43:33,013 --> 00:43:34,915
[gasping]

488
00:43:34,982 --> 00:43:36,884
Okay, okay, okay, okay.

489
00:43:38,252 --> 00:43:41,590
-[gasping and coughing]
-Here, put it back.

490
00:43:41,689 --> 00:43:43,558
-No. [gasping]
-It's okay.

491
00:43:43,691 --> 00:43:45,693
You gotta get me out of here,
KC.

492
00:43:45,693 --> 00:43:48,496
[wheezing] They know I got out.

493
00:43:48,563 --> 00:43:50,865
They don't want me to talk.

494
00:43:50,931 --> 00:43:53,100
-Raleigh coal?
-Please, KC.

495
00:43:53,167 --> 00:43:56,170
What happened, Bo?
Is Jesse alive?

496
00:43:56,237 --> 00:43:57,738
I don't know.

497
00:43:59,707 --> 00:44:01,742
That blackness in the earth,

498
00:44:02,910 --> 00:44:06,280
brushed up against
some greater dark.

499
00:44:06,347 --> 00:44:08,182
What?

500
00:44:08,249 --> 00:44:10,751
Don't let them open up
the mountain, KC.

501
00:44:11,385 --> 00:44:15,823
I closed it back up, but
you've seen what it done to me

502
00:44:15,890 --> 00:44:17,258
in just one second.

503
00:44:18,759 --> 00:44:21,228
Don't let it out.

504
00:44:22,163 --> 00:44:23,397
[coughing]

505
00:44:23,464 --> 00:44:25,366
-Hey!
-[heavy coughing]

506
00:44:25,432 --> 00:44:26,867
[gasping]

507
00:44:26,934 --> 00:44:28,802
-Get me out of here.
-Okay! Okay!

508
00:44:28,869 --> 00:44:31,506
I got Meemaw's spare breather
in the truck.

509
00:44:31,573 --> 00:44:33,207
I'll fetch it.

510
00:44:37,745 --> 00:44:39,180
[heavy coughing]

511
00:44:49,957 --> 00:44:51,325
Mrs. Scarbro.

512
00:44:55,296 --> 00:44:57,331
What brings you
to Kingwood today?

513
00:44:58,365 --> 00:44:59,767
And you are?

514
00:44:59,767 --> 00:45:01,335
My name is Eli.

515
